   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Hyperspace\n\nA jump to lightspeed: stars stretch into streaks around the outgoing scene, which is pushed toward the camera, then a white flash cuts to the incoming scene while the last streaks fade. Built-in placeholder scenes A and B (the two .hsp-panel elements) make it preview on its own; to use it between your own scenes, replace the contents of those two panels with your scenes (or set them to your full-frame clips) and keep the block on a track above.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 1.8667 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Sci-fi, space, gaming or tech launches that want an epic jump.\n- A hard, high-energy cut between two acts.\n\nAvoid when:\n- Realistic or documentary pieces.\n- Videos that already carry other flash or glitch transitions.\n\nVariables:\n- stars (number, 40-600): Stars, default 260\n- streak_color (color): Streak color, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- accent_color (color): Accent color, default \"#E5322D\"\n- accent_ratio (number, 0-1): Accent ratio, default 0.14\n- flash (boolean): Flash, default true\n- flash_color (color): Flash color, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
